  "checks": [
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.WaveKernel.waveHat: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:653 and claims.yaml:2326 match WaveKernel.lean:43-44, 's * Real.sinc (s * ‖ξ‖)', without restrictions. TeX:649-650 defines 'sin(s|ξ|)/|ξ|' with value s at zero in unlabelled prose. The real-valued representation agrees."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.WaveKernel.waveHat_continuous: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:654 and claims.yaml:2333 match WaveKernel.lean:47, 'Continuous fun z : ℝ × Rd d => ...', with no hypotheses. TeX:649-650 supplies the wave function but no joint-continuity lemma. Auxiliary classification is appropriate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.WaveKernel.waveHat_zero: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:655 and claims.yaml:2340 match WaveKernel.lean:53, 'waveHat s (0 : Rd d) = s', for arbitrary real s. TeX:650 explicitly says 'with value s at ξ = 0' in unlabelled prose."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.WaveKernel.waveHat_of_ne_zero: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:656 and claims.yaml:2347 match WaveKernel.lean:57-58, hypothesis 'ξ ≠ 0' and the sine quotient. TeX:649-650 gives that quotient away from zero, without a direct label."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.WaveKernel.abs_waveHat_le: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:657 and claims.yaml:2354 match WaveKernel.lean:66, '|waveHat s ξ| ≤ |s|', for all real s. TeX:719 uses '|Ĝ_s(ξ)| ≤ min(s,|ξ|⁻¹)' on positive time. The explicitly stated real-time extension is harmless."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.WaveKernel.abs_waveHat_le_inv: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:658 and claims.yaml:2361 match WaveKernel.lean:71-72, hypothesis 'ξ ≠ 0' and bound '1 / ‖ξ‖'. TeX:719 uses precisely this component of the minimum bound; the zero-frequency restriction avoids division by zero."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.WaveKernel.abs_waveHat_le_min: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:659 and claims.yaml:2368 match WaveKernel.lean:77-78, '0 ≤ s', 'ξ ≠ 0' and 'min s (1 / ‖ξ‖)'. TeX:719 states the same bound for the positive-time integrals."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.WaveKernel.waveHat_scaling: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:660 and claims.yaml:2375 match WaveKernel.lean:82-83, hypothesis '0 < θ' and factor 'θ⁻¹'. TeX:735-738 uses 'Ĝ_{u/θ}(θη) = θ⁻¹Ĝ_u(η)' under θ > 0. Constants and dilation direction agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.WaveKernel.abs_waveHat_mul_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:661 and claims.yaml:2382 match WaveKernel.lean:91-92, the unrestricted product bound with constant 2. TeX:719-729 instead splits low and high frequencies; it does not state this combined majorant. Auxiliary classification is correct."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.WaveKernel.waveHat_laplace: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:662 and claims.yaml:2389 match WaveKernel.lean:128-130, '0 < a', integrability on L0 and integral '1/(a²+‖ξ‖²)'. TeX:666-667 states the same transform in unlabelled prose. Zero frequency is included."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.integral_pos_of_ae_pos: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:663 and claims.yaml:2397 match TimeFractional.lean:59-61, 'Integrable f μ', 'μ ≠ 0' and '0 < f' almost everywhere. TeX:7625-7629 invokes positivity in the application but contains no general measure-space lemma. No direct label is appropriate."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.integrable_of_rpow_bounds: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:664 and claims.yaml:2404 match TimeFractional.lean:71-75: '-1 < p', 'q < -1', a.e. strong measurability and the two power bounds. TeX:7623-7625 gives application-specific asymptotics, not this general helper."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.subKernel_integrable: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:665 and claims.yaml:2411 match TimeFractional.lean:94-98, '0 < a', '0 < r' and integrability of λ^(a-1)e^(-rλ). TeX:7510-7511 uses this integrability in unlabelled prose. Auxiliary classification is reasonable."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.subKernel_nonneg: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:666 and claims.yaml:2418 match TimeFractional.lean:106-107, hypothesis '0 ≤ l', without restrictions on a or r. TeX:7504-7505 has the corresponding positive-domain integrand but no separate labelled nonnegativity statement."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.rpow_neg_eq_subordination: P:clock-copy-obstruction",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:667 and claims.yaml:2425 match TimeFractional.lean:112-113, '0 < a', '0 < r' and Gamma(a)^(-1). TeX:7604-7606 explicitly invokes the 'Laplace formula for the power covariance'; the manuscript's 0 < a < 1 lies within the Lean range."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.Psi: E:averaged-clock-kernel",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:668 and claims.yaml:2432 match TimeFractional.lean:123-127, including '-v*l²/2' and Gamma(a)^(-1). TeX:7502-7506 defines the same integral for 'r>0,v≥0'. Lean's totalized extension outside that domain does not change the manuscript object."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.psiKernel_measurable: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:669 and claims.yaml:2439 match TimeFractional.lean:130, 'Measurable (psiKernel a r v)', for arbitrary parameters. TeX:7504-7505 displays this integrand but has no separate measurability lemma. Auxiliary mapping is correct."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.psiKernel_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:670 and claims.yaml:2446 match TimeFractional.lean:134-135, '0 ≤ v', '0 ≤ l' and domination by subKernel. TeX:7510-7512 gives the resulting integral bound, not this separately stated pointwise helper."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.psiKernel_pos: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:671 and claims.yaml:2453 match TimeFractional.lean:142-143, requiring only '0 < l'. TeX:7504-7505 contains the positive integrand on λ > 0 but no direct labelled positivity lemma for it."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.psiKernel_integrable: E:averaged-clock-kernel",
      "verdict": "PASS_WITH_NOTES",
      "reason": "Ledger:672 and claims.yaml:2460 match TimeFractional.lean:146-147, '0 < a', '0 < r', '0 ≤ v'. TeX:7510-7511 justifies Fubini by the integrable exponential majorant. The cited ledger line numbers are shifted; see W8."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.Psi_zero: E:averaged-clock-kernel",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:673 and claims.yaml:2467 match TimeFractional.lean:155, '0 < a', '0 < r' and 'Psi a r 0 = r^(-a)'. TeX:7504-7509 gives the same specialization, including the variance-zero Gaussian interpretation. It is more precise than merely citing the upper bound."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.Psi_pos: E:averaged-clock-kernel",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:674 and claims.yaml:2474 match TimeFractional.lean:162, '0 < a', '0 < r', '0 ≤ v' and strict positivity. TeX:7512 states nonnegativity; strict positivity follows directly from its positive integrand at 7504-7505. This harmless strengthening is visible in the row."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.Psi_antitone: E:averaged-clock-kernel",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:675 and claims.yaml:2481 match TimeFractional.lean:170-171: '0 < a', '0 < r', '0 ≤ v', 'v ≤ v′'. TeX:7502 and 7512 specify the same domain and that Psi 'decreases with v'. Inequality direction agrees."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.Psi_le_rpow: E:averaged-clock-kernel",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:676 and claims.yaml:2488 match TimeFractional.lean:184-185, '0 < a', '0 < r', '0 ≤ v' and 'Psi a r v ≤ r^(-a)'. TeX:7512 states this exact bound."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.Psi_properties_paper: E:averaged-clock-kernel",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:677 and claims.yaml:2495 match TimeFractional.lean:191-196, including integrability, nonnegativity, antitonicity and the power bound under '0 < a', '0 < r', '0 ≤ v ≤ v′'. TeX:7502-7512 contains these properties on that domain."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeC_continuous: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:678 and claims.yaml:2502 match TimeFractional.lean:201-205, joint continuity for arbitrary complex a,b and real λ. TeX:7583-7602 integrates wave products rather than stating this general exponential-kernel continuity fact."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.integrable_exp_neg: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:679 and claims.yaml:2509 match TimeFractional.lean:209-211, hypothesis '0 < c' and exponential integrability on L0. TeX:7583-7602 uses exponential damping but has no direct label for this general helper."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeC_integrable: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:680 and claims.yaml:2516 match TimeFractional.lean:214-215, '0 < a.re', '0 < b.re', '0 ≤ lam'. TeX:7583-7602 treats a different, wave-product integrand. Auxiliary classification is correct."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeC_cone: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:681 and claims.yaml:2523 match TimeFractional.lean:227-228, requiring '0 < b.re', '0 ≤ lam', with arbitrary real s. TeX:7593-7598 instead evaluates a sine-containing cone integral. No direct label is correct."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeC_half_lt: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:682 and claims.yaml:2530 match TimeFractional.lean:250-255, '0 < b.re', '0 ≤ lam', '0 < s', and indicator t > s. TeX:7585 mentions the time cones but does not state this complex exponential half-cone identity."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeC_half_le: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:683 and claims.yaml:2537 match TimeFractional.lean:258-264, '0 < b.re', '0 ≤ lam', '0 < s', and indicator t ≥ s. TeX:7585 has no separate closed-half-cone exponential identity. The null boundary causes no discrepancy."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.integral_cexp_neg_Ioi: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:684 and claims.yaml:2544 match TimeFractional.lean:267-268, hypothesis '0 < z.re' and integral '1/z'. TeX:7583-7602 contains elementary damped integrations, but not this general complex statement."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeC_integral_lt: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:685 and claims.yaml:2551 match TimeFractional.lean:274-277, positive real parts, λ ≥ 0 and cone s < t, with value '1/(a+b)/(b+λ)'. TeX:7585-7601 computes wave-product cones, not this auxiliary formula."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeC_swap: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:686 and claims.yaml:2558 match TimeFractional.lean:291-295, unrestricted swapping of rates and coordinates. TeX:7601 adds the second cone but does not state this general kernel symmetry lemma."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeC_integral: P:clock-copy-obstruction",
      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "reason": "Fidelity holds: Ledger:687 and claims.yaml:2565 match TimeFractional.lean:299-303, '0 < a.re', '0 < b.re', '0 ≤ lam'. Mapping fails: TeX:7583-7602 evaluates 'e^{-θ(s+t)-λ|s-t|} Ĝ_s conjugate(Ĝ_t)' using sine integrals, not the general complex exponential identity. Relabel as a Lean-route auxiliary; W1."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeR_ofReal: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:688 and claims.yaml:2572 match TimeFractional.lean:346-347, unrestricted casting of twoTimeR to twoTimeC with a=b=c. TeX:7646-7653 uses q,w coordinates and a resolvent identity, not this cast lemma."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeR_pos: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:689 and claims.yaml:2579 match TimeFractional.lean:354, positivity for all real c,λ and coordinates. TeX:7646 invokes nonnegative Tonelli, but has no general real two-time exponential positivity lemma."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeR_integral: P:clock-copy-obstruction",
      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "reason": "Ledger:690 and claims.yaml:2586 faithfully summarize TimeFractional.lean:357-358, '0 < c', '0 ≤ lam', integral '1/(c(c+lam))'. TeX:7646-7648 instead integrates q to '2(1-e^{-Aw})/A'. The manuscript does not use this two-time lemma; W1."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.twoTimeR_lintegral: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:691 and claims.yaml:2593 match TimeFractional.lean:375-379, '0 < c', '0 ≤ lam' and the ENNReal lower-integral identity. TeX:7646 invokes Tonelli without this lower-integral formulation. Auxiliary classification is correct."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.iterated_integral_swap: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:692 and claims.yaml:2600 match TimeFractional.lean:386-391, '[SFinite μX]', '[SFinite μY]', '[SFinite μZ]' and 'Integrable F'. TeX:7583 and 7646 invoke Fubini/Tonelli in specific applications, not this arbitrary-space rearrangement."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.TimeFractional.lintegral_triple_twoTime: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PARTIAL",
      "reason": "TimeFractional.lean:406-413 assumes '[SFinite ν]', '[SFinite μ]' and measurability of each of f,c,A, besides their signs. Ledger:693 and claims.yaml:2607 omit the measure hypotheses and do not clearly distribute measurability across all three functions. TeX:7646's 'nonnegative Tonelli' does not justify an arbitrary-measure version. Auxiliary mapping itself is right; W3."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.SpectralHomogeneous: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:694 and claims.yaml:2615 match SpectralHomog.lean:59-61: every measurable A and '0 < c' satisfy 'μ(c • A)=ofReal(c^alpha)*μ A'. TeX:704-705 derives exactly 'μ(cA)=c^αμ(A)'; TeX:4522-4525 confirms the quantifiers. The supplied input is not stronger."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.map_smul_eq: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:695 and claims.yaml:2622 match SpectralHomog.lean:66-67, 'SpectralHomogeneous μ alpha', '0 < c', and pushforward factor c^(-alpha). TeX:704-705's set scaling and TeX:4522-4525's explicit pushforward description give this same equivalent identity."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.integral_comp_smul: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:696 and claims.yaml:2629 match SpectralHomog.lean:74-76, 'SpectralHomogeneous', '0 < c', 'Measurable f' and factor c^(-alpha). TeX:734-738 uses this change of spectral variables for finite integrals. Lean additionally permits totalized nonintegrable cases; this does not alter the paper-domain identity."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.measure_ball: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:697 and claims.yaml:2636 match SpectralHomog.lean:82-83, spectral homogeneity and '0 < r'. TeX:706 states 'μ(B_r)=r^α V' with V=μ(B_1). Ball scaling and exponent agree."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.measure_zero: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:698 and claims.yaml:2643 match SpectralHomog.lean:89-90, 'SpectralHomogeneous', '[IsLocallyFiniteMeasure μ]', '0 < alpha'. TeX:705-706 explicitly uses 'Radon finiteness and α > 0' to conclude 'μ({0})=0'."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.integrable_of_le_inv: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:699 and claims.yaml:2650 match SpectralHomog.lean:105-108, integrable resolvent majorant, a.e. strong measurability and the pointwise K-bound. TeX:719-729 uses different concrete bounds and has no general domination lemma."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.integrable_inv_one_add_sq: L:damped-homogeneous-norms",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:700 and claims.yaml:2657 match SpectralHomog.lean:112-114, spectral homogeneity, local finiteness and 'alpha < 2'. TeX:709-713 proves the resolvent integral finite under '0 < α < 2'. The explicitly stated Lean generalization does not require the unused lower bound."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.resolvent: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:701 and claims.yaml:2664 match SpectralHomog.lean:173, '∫ ξ, 1/(q²+‖ξ‖²) ∂μ'. TeX:7519 defines the same R_Gamma in unlabelled setup, used for q > 0. No Fourier normalization factor is missing."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.heat: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:702 and claims.yaml:2671 match SpectralHomog.lean:176, exponential '-w*‖ξ‖²/2'. TeX:7517-7518 defines h_Gamma by exactly that spectral integral for w > 0. The physical heat-average identification is separately excluded from formalization."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.resolvent_integrable: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:703 and claims.yaml:2678 match SpectralHomog.lean:179-180, integrable (1+‖ξ‖²)^(-1) and 'q ≠ 0'. TeX:7521 says the resolvent is finite for 'q>0'. The broader q-range is explicit and harmless because the denominator depends on q²."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.heat_integrable: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:704 and claims.yaml:2685 match SpectralHomog.lean:195-197, integrable resolvent majorant and '0 < w'. TeX:7521 states heat-mass finiteness for 'w,q>0'. These are unlabelled setup facts."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.resolvent_homog: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:705 and claims.yaml:2692 match SpectralHomog.lean:225-226, spectral homogeneity and '0 < q', yielding q^(alpha-2)R(1). TeX:7521-7523 states that same formula in unlabelled prose."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.heat_homog: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:706 and claims.yaml:2699 match SpectralHomog.lean:244-245, spectral homogeneity and '0 < w', yielding w^(-alpha/2)h(1). TeX:7521-7522 states the identical homogeneity in unlabelled prose."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.resolvent_sub_pos: P:clock-copy-obstruction",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:707 and claims.yaml:2706 match SpectralHomog.lean:260-262, integrable resolvent majorant, 'μ ≠ 0', '0 < q', 'q < q′'. TeX:7625-7627 explicitly states 'R(θ)-R(θ+λ)>0, since μ≠0'. The general q,q′ formulation faithfully covers this step."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.resolvent_pos: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:708 and claims.yaml:2713 match SpectralHomog.lean:274-278, integrable majorant, 'μ ≠ 0', 'q ≠ 0'. TeX:7514-7521 assumes nonzero covariance and states positivity for q > 0 in unlabelled setup. The extension to negative q is harmless."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.heat_pos: no direct label",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:709 and claims.yaml:2720 match SpectralHomog.lean:281-284, integrable majorant, 'μ ≠ 0', '0 < w'. TeX:7514-7521 assumes nonzero covariance and states heat-mass positivity for w > 0."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.SpectralHomog.spectral_ne_zero: P:clock-copy-obstruction",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Ledger:710 and claims.yaml:2727 match SpectralHomog.lean:289-290, locally finite Γ, 'IsSpectralMeasure Γ μ', 'Γ ≠ 0'. TeX:7514 assumes nonzero covariance and TeX:7627 uses 'μ≠0'. The Lean spectral convention at HomogHypothesis.lean:52-55 agrees with TeX:173-176."
    },
    {
